Piles of Boxes
https://docs.google.com/document/d/1k0mOvFj-PT6LvbUjTrw9O-u7lHAMrAUMu2vE7VLp5F0/edit?tab=t.0
Intuition: In one operation, we can only reduce the tallest pile to the next tallest height.
Since we can only decrease heights, all piles will eventually become equal to the smallest height.
Whenever the height changes while moving from right to left,
all taller piles must be reduced one more time.

Code: 
class Solution {

    public static long pilesOfBoxes(int[] boxesInPiles) {

        Arrays.sort(boxesInPiles);

        long steps = 0;
        int n = boxesInPiles.length;

        for(int i = n - 1; i > 0; i--){

            if(boxesInPiles[i] != boxesInPiles[i - 1]){

                steps += (n - i);

            }
        }

        return steps;
    }
}
